TEXTS AND TRANSLATIONS

Shown exactly as published, never edited. The site's catalogue (web/public/data/catalog.json) is
built from these collections, each pinned to one commit:

- Perseus Digital Library, Tufts University: canonical-greekLit (PerseusDL/canonical-greekLit,
  commit bcc5df0602f3b3fe6fefe1e1d575602a25ab1db6). CC BY-SA 4.0. doi:10.5281/zenodo.596309.
  Perseus asks that any modifications be offered back to Perseus.
- Open Greek and Latin, First Thousand Years of Greek (OpenGreekAndLatin/First1KGreek,
  commit 8ee111eb44ecef4120c844e10749178d95d1f30c). CC BY-SA 4.0. doi:10.5281/zenodo.596723.
- The editor and translator of each text, as named in that text file's header.

Left out: the Coptic Gospel of Mark (urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0031.tlg002.1st1K-cop1), licensed
"for academic use only". Texts left out for their licence are listed in pipeline/not_open.tsv.


WORDS AND DICTIONARIES

- GLAUx, by Alek Keersmaekers: word analyses, sentence structure, and each work's genre, dialect and
  date. CC BY-SA 4.0; some source texts and hand annotations inside GLAUx carry other licences,
  listed in GLAUx's metadata. Keersmaekers, A. (2021), "The GLAUx corpus: methodological issues in
  designing a long-term, diverse, multi-layered corpus of Ancient Greek", Proceedings of the 2nd
  International Workshop on Computational Approaches to Historical Language Change, 39-50.
- Liddell-Scott-Jones Greek-English Lexicon (LSJ): Text provided under a CC BY-SA license by Perseus
  Digital Library, http://www.perseus.tufts.edu, with funding from The National Endowment for the
  Humanities. Data accessed from https://github.com/PerseusDL/lexica/.
- Dickinson College Commentaries Greek Core Vocabulary, by Christopher Francese and collaborators.
  CC BY-SA 3.0.
- hypotactic.com scansions, by David Chamberlain. CC BY 4.0.
- Wikidata (authors' dates, places, descriptions, names). CC0.
- Princeton WordNet 3.0. WordNet 3.0 Copyright 2006 by Princeton University. All rights reserved.
  Under the WordNet licence: https://wordnet.princeton.edu/license-and-commercial-use
- Wiktionary, fetched live in the visitor's browser. CC BY-SA 4.0.


